id: pm-abvpgh
title: Patch transitive Hono advisories in the MCP Apps dependency graph
description: "Remediate three individually tracked Hono advisories newly returned by the final registry audit. Keep the supported Node floor and release-age policy, update the shared Hono 4.x dependency floor, and verify the real MCP consumers and release gates."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: changelog-exclude,dependencies,mcp,security
created_at: "2026-09-09T00:11:32.913Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-09T00:24:02.745Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-09T00:24:02.110Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-09T00:24:02.110Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: Each advisory has an individually triageable child with source and severity; all Hono resolutions are patched; audit and frozen install pass; MCP and full release verification pass.
parent: pm-qwoy
resolution: "Enforced Hono >=4.13.5 <5.0.0 and regenerated the lockfile at 4.13.7, removing the three reported Hono advisories while retaining runtime support and release-age policy."
expected_result: "The vulnerable Hono versions are excluded; dependency audit is clean, frozen installation is reproducible and MCP consumers and repository verification pass."
actual_result: "Patched graph verification: all 8623 tests in 653 files pass at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with zero uncovered counts: 63729 statements, 48461 branches, 13216 functions and 61134 lines. All four TypeScript projects and every linked audit, frozen-install and real MCP workflow/HTTP/Apps/transport check pass. pnpm audit reports zero advisories and pnpm why resolves only Hono 4.13.7. Documentation, structural/docstring, graph-composition and record-integrity gates pass. Final pushed-head hosted checks, full platform matrix, preflight and full review govern merge."
